column9:
CoreLogic Solutions, LLC focuses primarily on property-related data, particularly as available in publicly available records. In connection with our products and services, we may collect and transfer the following:

•	Identifiers, such as names, telephone numbers, and addresses; 
•	Commercial information, such as information relating to buying, selling, owning, or renting property, including financial information and records reflecting consumer interests, purchasing tendencies, behavioral tendencies, and lifestyle preferences; 
•	Demographic information, such as education, language preference, age, and marital status; and
•	Geolocation data, such as city, state, country of residence, and postal code.

The categories of data we process and transfer include: (Please note that examples may not be applicable to every individual.)

Personal Identifiers (e.g., name, birth year, mailing address, phone number, voter registration); 

Financial Information (e.g., loan type, mortgage amount, lender name); 

Characteristics of Protected Classifications (e.g., gender, age, marital status, veteran status); 

Commercial Information (e.g., property location & characteristics, dwelling type, property value, vehicle make/model/year, move-in date ); 

Employment/Professional Information (e.g., occupation); 

Health Information (e.g., ailments); 

Internet & network information (e.g., browsing history, IP address, data collected by cookies and similar technologies, Site interactions, device information such as device IDs, specifications, and operating system); 

Geolocation Data (e.g., latitude & longitude of residence); 

Inferences drawn from the above categories of Personal Information that relate to your preferences, characteristics, psychological trends, predispositions, behavior, attitudes, intelligence, abilities, and aptitudes (e.g., value scores, net worth models, interests, familial relationships, milestones such as engagement or pregnancy, purchase likelihood models).

Depending on the consumer (and depending on whether the consumer is a client of ours or a member of the public with whom we lack a direct relationship), we may disclose the following categories of information for such purposes which may be considered a sale (as defined by applicable law): identifiers, interests and demographics;
inferenced data, such as whether you may be likely to purchase certain goods in the near future, or information about your demographics (e.g., estimated age or income range).

To opt out of this type of sale, please go to https://unsubscribe.stirista.com/ and follow the instructions on the web page.

Personal and online identifiers (such as first and last name, email address, demographic information, mailing or physical address, voter registration status, voting history, statistical and market area information, area selection data, lifestyle and wealth data, political contribution information, census data, and other voter-related information, or unique online identifiers);
Characteristics of legally protected classifications (such as gender or age);
Commercial or transactions information (such as records of personal and real property or products or services purchased, obtained, or considered);
Internet or other electronic network activity information (such as browsing history, search history, interactions with a website, email, application, or advertisement);
Geolocation information (such as mailing and physical address but excluding precise geolocation data);
Professional or employment-related information;
Education information;
Inferences drawn from the above information about predicted characteristics and preferences; and
Other information that is linked to the personal information above.

Identifiers;
Vehicle Information;
Commercial information;
Internet or other network activity information; and
Inferences drawn from other personal information.

Growing Libraries receives and handles data from various third parties. The categories of data that we process and transfer are:

•	Personal and online identifiers (such as first and last name, postal address, telephone number, email address, or unique online identifiers);
•	Characteristics of protected classifications under relevant law (examples: age, marital status, sex);
•	Commercial or transactions information (such as records of personal or real property or products or services purchased, obtained or considered, vehicle information);
•	Internet or other electronic network activity information (such as interactions with a website, email, application, or advertisement);
•	Professional or employment-related information; and
•	Inferences drawn from the above information about your predicted characteristics and preferences.

